{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"agent_message","text":"A useful exact-layout optimization emerged: storing the four intermediate gradients interleaved as `[M, 4, 256]` lets one 2-D reduction compute all four biases with exactly the same reduction tree—even at `M=512`, where the earlier batched reduction changed rounding. rocBLAS also produces bit-identical GEMMs with the corresponding strides. I’m testing this locally because it removes six launches from every 512-token workload without relaxing correctness."}}
